  "slug": "edna-diversity-monkfish-759e",
  "summary": "Recent preprints pair eDNA monitoring with sample-handling tests and integrative taxonomy to refine marine biodiversity inference.",
  "synthesis": "The dominant thread is molecular inference of biodiversity from environmental samples and specimens. A freezing experiment shows that storing seawater samples for one month lowered eDNA-inferred marine invertebrate richness and altered community composition, with Pseudocalanus copepods among the notably affected taxa, indicating that preservation choices can bias metabarcoding-based estimates. A Cook Inlet time series applies eDNA metabarcoding and qPCR to track endangered beluga whale occurrence alongside salmonid and eulachon prey dynamics. Separately, integrative molecular and geometric morphometric analyses of Lophius gastrophysus across the western Atlantic support two distinct lineages, an example of taxonomic resolution that does not rely on eDNA. What is new is the direct attention to sampling protocol effects and to multi-taxon eDNA time series.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-haiku-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-11-19"
}
